{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790973743,"nonce":"9Y/B7l9ID8/LtLrYRx9EcOvBseE=","title":"Hot reload cannot add a closure or method","message":"A reload that adds a function shifts every later findex, so it is refused (\"the function table changed shape\"). For UI work this is the most common edit: adding a reactive expression or a handler to a template adds a closure. ashui's tests/fixtures/hotreload/run.sh v3 is the reproducer (one added () -\u003e Single closure). Supporting it means matching old and new functions by identity rather than findex, remapping the function table, closures and vtables, and keeping frames of the old bodies valid. Follows 67bd802, which made the refusal reliable.","files":null}]}